Check ONE file: @FILE@ in the verse repository.

Your working directory holds the repository as a subdirectory — the brief above names it — so
the file is at <repo>/@FILE@.

Find the references in that file that no longer resolve against the tree, and fix them. A
reference is anything the prose asserts exists in the code: a function or type name, a file
path, a CLI flag, an HTTP route, a make target, an environment variable. It "no longer
resolves" when the thing named is absent, or is named differently, or the file describes a
signature or behaviour the code contradicts.

Check every such reference in that file, and only that file. Do not go looking for work
elsewhere: another file's problems are another task's.

Only report what you have checked against the tree. A claim you could not verify is not a
finding — say so instead of guessing. Do not rewrite prose you merely disagree with: this is
about references that are FALSE, not about style.

Read <repo>/docs/working/contributing.md first and hold to it.

Leave the tree building. Edit the file and stop — do not commit, and do not run the full test
suite: a single file's references are checkable by reading the code they name, and this task is
meant to be short.

Your final message IS the answer. Write the account first — what you changed and why each was
wrong, with the line and the evidence — and end it with the block the answer contract asks for.
`status: clean` if the file was already right and you changed nothing, which is a real result
and not a failure; `status: fixed` if you changed it.
